Gryphonline is a logistics and mail company. Its name comes from the flock of griffins it keeps for delivery work, flying in and out of a roost below the buildings from a cliff roughly a hundred feet above the river. The company says the griffins are well trained and fed at the facility, and would not take a bird.

Its distribution center is a griffin nesting site and mail office, an established building with an interior plaza, a red and orange-leaved tree at its center, and signs pointing out the self-serve mail and P.O. boxes, the counter for sending packages, and an employees-only service area. The address is where [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]] keeps its headquarters, P.O. Box 9C, and also where the signal from the radar dish taken off the roller rink appears to originate.
